Sincerest apologies for the delay in contacting you on this ticket, this is due to change in contractor. I am picking this ticket up from Clarissa.

Under paragraph 3.1.8 of our Contract Review and Delegated Signatory Authority, employment contracts or consultancy contracts as well as any agreement to amend or terminate the employment contract or consultancy contract in the name and on behalf of any Group Entity will *require your approval prior to signing*. In accordance with paragraph 5.1.2, the management bodies of Group Entities have already approved the following delegations of signatory authority for employment or consultancy contracts as well as any agreement to amend or terminate (unilaterally or otherwise) the employment or consultancy contract:

(a) Country Manager - for employees or consultants employed in respective country;

(b) Expansion Manager - for employees or consultants employed by Group Entities of their region;

(c) HQ Head of Division - for employees or consultants employed into their reporting line regardless of employing Group Entity;

(d) Head of People & Culture - for all employees and consultants regardless of their reporting line or employing Group Entity;

(e) Head of Legal in HQ - for all employees and consultants regardless of their reporting line or employing Group Entity.

So the delegated authorised signatories as stated (a)-(e) above will require your prior approval, which once obtained can sign employment or consultancy contracts on Bolt’s behalf and so a power of attorney for the purpose of signing employment or consultancy contracts is not required. 

Therefore this ticket can be closed but before I do close this ticket, are there are any other reasons behind your requirement for a PoA? If so, please do let me know, and if a PoA is required, I will rope in my colleague covering Malta and Cyprus too.

I have also sent you a Slack msg and am looking forward to your reply.

Many thanks

