Hey Przemysław, let’s answer it in backward order. 

{quote}Is the Airflow DAG looking at the past dates if data from present days has already been processed?{quote}

Nope. It runs sequentially every hour and expects that the full data for the previous hour has been already produced. 

{quote}So in other words, if I started sending messages with dates from April, do I need to set the {{start_date}} to April?{quote}

Yes. It will create airflow job schedule starting from the given date. 

{quote}is it fine to use past event timestamps here (several months old)?{quote}

Yes, it is fine. 

{quote}Will it work just fine if I started publishing event buffer messages from past events?{quote}

Well, to achieve the desired result i would suggest you to implement everything except for Airflow step (or implement and deploy but switch it off) and start producing events. Does not really matter what order. 

Once all historical records are pushed and real-time data flows smoothly - deploy and enable Airflow DAG. 

But please be gentle with producing events. They go to Kafka and it might not be ready for an explosive usage pattern. *What is the daily amount of events btw? And how big is the history?*

Also, be aware that Kafka retention period is 3 days. So you need to enable DAG within that period. 

