Hi Rea.

I see that this is indeed an abuser. I noticed that the user literally has a CS note in the profile for all of his 7 last orders. However, the Fraud team is not taking action against refund/promo diggers individually. We’re looking for bigger patterns. Appreciate the effort, but there is no need to escalate these single users. A note in the profile should be enough for CS to be more careful when dealing with contacts from this person. A hard block wouldn’t be needed here, as the only action necessary is just to deny future refunds when there’s no clear indication that the user actually requires one. 


{quote}Is it even possible to make a new account when so many fraud accounts are connected to it?{quote}

Yes, it’s possible. Fraud doesn’t stop account creation at any point. What our fraud engine does is give risk score to users based on the data we have which will potentially lead to an action. 

{quote}Can they all be blocked?{quote}

No. There’s no reason to hard block all related users due to one confirmed abuser. It’s again up to CS to improve the process to prevent this sort of social engineering abuse.

