Hi Shiv,
We don’t currently have any other properties with this supplier. Please see the below r.e. your comments:

* *Term:* commencing today with a 3 month term that automatically extends on a rolling basis on 4 January 2023 or on the renewed End Date following an extension if notice to terminate is not provided by Bolt. {color:#ff5630}-Correct, rather than a monthly rolling, it will be a 3 monthly rolling- this gave us a better price{color}
* *Notice period in accordance with the Special Condition:* Bolt would need to provide one months’ written notice in advance of the End Date to terminate this agreement so e.g. if Bolt wants to end the arrangement on 4 January 2023 without it being automatically renewed, it will need to provide notice by 3 December 2022 to ensure that the agreement terminates on 4 January 2023. I am assuming that this arrangement works for Bolt, but please do correct me if I am wrong.{color:#ff5630}- Yes this works, most of these rolling ones just continue unless we get the instruction to terminate, then we provide 1 month notice{color}
* *Ascent can terminate on or after 4 January 2023 by providing one month’s notice:* this means that after the 4th January 2023, Bolt may be left in a position where it has to find an alternative premises at such short notice. Would this be possible? {color:#ff5630}-This kind of stuff can’t be spoken for, we would just be forced to look elsewhere{color}
* *Ascent can terminate by providing one week’s written notice in the event of Bolt being in significant breach:* although Ascent’s early termination right in clause 9.1 is only in the event that Bolt commits a significant breach, this is not ideal as Bolt would be required to find alternative premises at very short notice. I am assuming that Markian is happy with this but in future, I would recommend obtaining mutual termination rights.  {color:#ff5630}-I again doubt we will find ourselves in a significant breach given that this is a unmanned office, but if you want this amended let me know. {color}
* *Repair obligations*: clause 7.2 puts an obligation on us to clean, repair and make good any damage to the area that we demise at our expense. Normally I would push back on this clause as we should not be accepting to repair or to make good damage to a premises that we do not own or have a legal interest in. However, given the urgency of this ticket and that this is an unmanned office and the chances of us causing and repairing damage are low, I would consider this low risk. If we have agreed any works to be undertaken to the premises we are also responsible for removing those works and reinstating the premises identical to as it was before the works were undertaken. I am assuming that Markian is alert to these repair obligations and that we are not carrying out any alteration works to this unmanned office, and therefore consider this to be low risk, but please do bear this obligation in mind if we do decide to make any alterations in future.  - {color:#ff5630}Noted{color}
* *Automatic fees renewal:* On each anniversary of the Start Date or renewal, Ascent may carry out reviews of the Licence Fee and Additional Services Charges and can automatically increase the fees under this agreement to the higher of the passing sum or the fee obtainable on a comparable open market agreement. Bolt is liable to pay any subsequent adjustment to the deposit to take account of any increase in the Total Fees following renewal. This is a regular rent review and ideally, we should not be agreeing to rent increases. We should in such circumstances, either have a right to terminate or have a capped amount that the rent can be increased to, but I am assuming that the risk here that Bolt’s rent may be reviewed as often as every three months has been considered but please do correct me if I am wrong.  - {color:#ff5630}Unsure of what action you’d like me to take here, but I’m assuming there would be reviews{color}
* *Indemnity*: Bolt are providing an indemnity for any costs or charges that may arise as a result of non payment of providing Additional Service Charges but as we haven’t signed up to receive any Additional Services, I consider this low risk, but if we do in future, bear in mind that we will be responsible for any costs or charges that may arise from non-payment of Additional Services Charges. - {color:#ff5630}Noted{color}
* *Risk assessments:* we are obliged to undertake risk assessments of activities and provide copies to Ascent free of Charge. Do you know what is required in relation to undertaking risk assessments for an unmanned office for Bolt? Given that this is unmanned and a short term tenancy for three months, it may not be applicable and so we can probably leave the wording in clause 7.9 in here for the time being as dormant. But we should know what is required from us in relation to risk assessments so, as an action point for future agreements with Ascent, do raise this with Ascent to determine the extent of our obligations.  - {color:#ff5630}I can raise this {color}
* *Required insurance levels:* we are responsible for maintaining adequate contents insurance, public liability insurance and any other insurances as required by the law and as the business demands but Ascent have not specified insurance levels. Bolt probably has the required insurance levels to cover loss or liabilities for a short term arrangement in any case, but in future, it would be beneficial to know exactly what levels of insurance are required from us to fully determine risk. - {color:#ff5630}We would have our own insurance i.e. public liability insurance{color}
* *Business rates:* Bolt is required to register with the appropriate authority for all Business Rates pertaining to the premises from early occupation or commencement to the end of this Agreement and ensure that all Business Rates are paid directly to the appropriate authority, irrespective of the Bolt’s occupation of the premises. Bolt must provide evidence of payment to Ascent. This is our responsibility to pay Business Rates and keep track of it. - {color:#ff5630}Noted{color}
* *Additional fees:* please bear in mind that according to clause 11, we will be penalised by late payment fees, an administration fee of £150 plus VAT, and interest, at a rate of 8% above base rate. There are also additional fees for repair and mail holding. -{color:#ff5630} Noted{color}
* *Guarantor:* I note the guarantor provisions are not relevant, given if it is a short term arrangement, we won’t push for clause 10 to be removed but if this was a more long term arrangement, we should ask for this clause to be removed. - {color:#ff5630}Noted{color}

